        "text": "<p>NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is a coenzyme found in every cell, which cells use to turn food into usable energy and to run maintenance processes such as DNA repair. Your body makes it continuously from precursors like vitamin B3 and nicotinamide riboside, and recycles it as it’s used.<\/p>"
